didn't expect to  be as funny as it was i was laughing out  loud a lot and  that humor was very strange which i  liked so i'm happy they were confident  enough to do that because that isn't the  most popular type of humor where you're  having hot dog fingers up here which  made me laugh so hard i loved everything  by the way with a hot dog finger  timeline with michellio and jamie lee  curtis that was something i'll never  forget especially the scenes when she's  playing piano with the feet and then  michellio puts her feet up to touch  jamie lee curtis that was just  comedy gold and  a lot of stuff like that happens this  film that's like completely random and  weird especially the whole rat tattooing  reference joke which is great because  it's not even like a recent film but  it's still just hysterical and they had  the raccoon  so so funny and there was humorous  moments that  got the crowd to laugh out loud like  literally a roar which i didn't even  remember experiencing since like borat  won in theaters or people laughing that  hard and those two scenes really were  actually it was just a small moment but  when evelyn  actually wipes her grandpa's snot and  puts it back in his mouth i thought that  was brilliant and also when  we get this fight sequence and these two  guys literally  have  these big plugs coming out of their  butts hanging out of their butts uh and  she's fighting them while it's hanging  out i mean the crowd was going nuts just  of laughter how insane that scene was so  really really awesome now it's  interesting as i was watching the film  it reminded me of one of my favorite  films of all time 2001 a space odyssey  and what i mean by that is that it's  just view of life right how small we are  in such a big universe i got that same  vibe and  it really leans to that and it's funny  because it actually referenced a space  odyssey in the scene with the apes in  this film so you can see that there  definitely was some inspiration there  but i love that  they didn't go as bleak as that in the  sense of they were acknowledging this is  the reality of the world how crazy the  world is with this whole everything  bagel  symbolism going on in all the circles  right everything going from that worked  really well and that  in the end they  still acknowledge that's the world we're  in but it's better to address it by  being kind and that's what really worked  for me because this movie did the  opposite where so many films end with  the big action scene at the end and then  you fight the villain and you kick the  villain's butt and use violence to win  where this saved all its action for the  middle so at the end when you think it's  gonna be this big fight scene she's  actually  killing them with kindness in the sense  right like hugging them you see all  these people are hurting for something  and that being kind is the best way to  go and i like that it showed the husband  wasn't naive that he believed in being  kind too so that really was just a great  message and about how like it real that  film is in the sense of his message that  this is how messed up the world can be  but there is something still to  appreciate about love about being  present about being kind to everybody  and even that the mother and daughter in  their relationship that they couldn't  see eye to eye but just being together  was enough right appreciating that and  that you're never gonna have this  perfect thing where you're totally  synced and that you have to kind of have  just sympathy for each other i thought  was really really just powerful and even  one of my favorite things was the rocks  when they had the mom and the daughter  as the rocks the first time we saw them  as a rocks was probably my favorite  moment of the film how quiet it was and  eerie it was with the captions and it  was the most powerful scene i thought of  the film that conversation the mom and  daughter had as rocks which is just  crazy but it worked but that's what was  really cool was the blend of genres here  from comedy to action a martial arts  film like the kung fu action was awesome  like those sequences looked amazing and  it was really exciting but it was such a  cool blend of genre because it was rapid  fire with the editing where it would go  from serious to action to humor and you  just didn't know what was coming next  and i think that's definitely part of  what kept you on the edge of your seat  now michelio's been being praised a lot  and she totally deserves it just  spectacular here i mean  everything she has to hit here playing  so many versions of her say himself but  different emotions just to play in the  main core of evelyn just hits them all  out of the park so really cool to see  that and i like it had you know meta  references to her with crouching tiger  hidden dragon but also to kiki kwan you  know with the  fanny pack and having the technology  like data from goonies that was that  love letter part of it to those actors  and even they brought in some horror in  it and some stuff that made me really  into this film was really when the  daughter first appears as this jobu  dupaki  character and  that moment when the mom's realizing  that and the fear she has and that  close-up on her and again how it just  shifts then to humor with the everything  bagel being the metaphor i thought was  great and of course jamie lee curtis i  mean transformative part and she just  does what is asked of her and kills it  per usual so that was great too and  now not everything is amazing to me here  i think the only thing i'll bring my  score down a little bit from being a 10  i want it to be a 10  but  there was a couple things i do think  that i don't know if this would take  points off the score but maybe it went  two wilds with the metaverse stuff and  all that traveling and verse jumping for  it to make any sense to any audience i  mean even a smart audience it's a lot i  mean it's almost just too ridiculous at  points where you're kind of like okay  you know what it's better i to enjoy  this one was not even trying to  understand all that i believe so that's  what i did so i don't really hold it  against the film i don't think it was  trying to make it to be so accurate or  understanding but i do think it could  have been a little more easier to grasp  for sure so that was something that took  me off a bit and  the bigger two points though was  i do believe the moment with the  daughter  and her hugging at the end would have  hit harder if i feel like they just gave  a little more time to the relationship  with the daughter of her at the  beginning of the film where i don't  think it was enough i think it was still  so distant for us as the audience to  understand that relationship that it  wasn't given enough time to really get  it and that  took away  from it landing so much and totally  understanding what was really the weight  of the conflict between the mother and  daughter there you get it from a surface  level but i wanted more i want a little  more time to dedicate that to set that  up to pay off more and  my last criticism is it did feel like  the movie was stacking on endings where  it was like  maybe this is where the run time was all  so long too where it was like it felt  like it ended four times and obviously  one time was purposeful it was like a  fake out with the credits which i  thought was great but it just kept going  in these moments that were like dramatic  like learning about the husband and him  not being naive then it would do another  thing and another type of ending feel  like we're just getting like is that it  is that it like it almost played with  your emotions too much or it was like  okay i feel like i've had my cathartic  moment here  and the film you know it kept doing  endings over and over in a sense which i  wasn't crazy about and i think that hurt  just the whole pacing of the film for to  feel like a total masterpiece but i do  think again this is a movie that is  incredible so i'm giving it a 9.6  i  loved it and for me it's definitely the  movie the year so far  for sure and i think it probably will  stay that way and it's going to be tough  to beat but who knows but again editing  acting  is just spectacular and really humor for  me here i laughed so much during this  film which was a treat and i was like i  was not expecting that much from this  type of film so i definitely recommend  it for everybody please let me know your  thoughts in the comments below i'd love  to hear them i read every comment try to  respond as many as i can please make  sure to subscribe you don't miss one of  my movie reviews i also do tv reviews  and celebrity interviews as well and  please follow me at steve varley show on  twitter instagram and tick tock for more  of me and i'll see you next time

